# 🕒 IBM Cognos Analytics Tutorial: How to Create and Schedule a Job

This tutorial will guide you through the step-by-step process of **creating and scheduling a job** in IBM Cognos Analytics.  
Follow each step carefully, using the screenshots provided for reference.

---

## Step 1 – Go to the Directory and Choose *Customer Satisfaction Report*
![](3.%20go%20to%20the%20directory%20and%20choose%20Customer%20Satisfaction%20Report.png)
Navigate to your content directory and locate the **Customer Satisfaction Report**. This is the report you’ll use for the scheduled job.

---

## Step 2 – Choose *Team Content*
![](2.%20choose%20team%20content.png)
Go to **Team Content** to access shared reports available in your organization.

---

## Step 3 – Choose the Hamburger Menu and Click *New Job*
![](4.%20choose%20hamburger%20menu%20and%20click%20new%20job.png)
Open the **hamburger menu (☰)** and select **New Job** to start creating a job.

---

## Step 4 – Add a Job Step
![](5.%20add%20job%20step.png)
In the Job editor, click **Add Step** to specify which report or process will be included in this job.

---

## Step 5 – Click *Financial* and Continue to Find *Customer Satisfaction Report*
![](6.%20click%20financial%20and%20continue%20untuk%20find%20the%20customer%20satisfaction%20report.png)
Browse through the **Financial** folder or the relevant directory to find the **Customer Satisfaction Report**.

---

## Step 6 – Choose *Customer Satisfaction Report*
![](7.%20choose%20customer%20satisfaction%20report.png)
Select the **Customer Satisfaction Report** to include it as a step in your job.

---

## Step 7 – Click *Edit* on the Right Side of the Job That Was Just Created
![](8.%20Click%20edit%20on%20the%20right%20side%20of%20the%20job%20that%20is%20just%20created.png)
Once the job appears in your list, click the **Edit (✏️)** icon to open the job configuration.

---

## Step 8 – Choose Default Format and Tick *Send Report via Email*
![](9.%20choose%20default%20format%20and%20tick%20send%20report%20via%20email.png)
In the job details, set the **default output format** (e.g., PDF or Excel) and check **Send report via email**.

---

## Step 9 – Insert the Email in the Details
![](10.%20insert%20the%20email%20in%20the%20details%20.png)
Add the recipient’s **email address** where the report will be sent after the job runs.

---

## Step 10 – Save the Job
![](11.%20save%20the%20job.png)
Click **Save** to confirm and store your job configuration.

---

## Step 11 – Create a New Schedule
![](12.%20create%20a%20new%20schedule.png)
Click on **Create Schedule** to set up when and how often the job will run.

---

## Step 12 – Save the Schedule
![](13.%20save%20the%20schedule.png)
After defining your schedule (e.g., daily, weekly, or monthly), click **Save** to finalize it.

---

## ✅ Step 13 – Schedule Job Completed!
Your **Customer Satisfaction Report job** is now successfully created and scheduled.  
You will receive the report automatically via email based on the schedule you configured.

---

### 💡 Tips
- You can manage all your scheduled jobs under **My Content → Schedules**.  
- Make sure the report runs correctly before automating it.  
- Modify or disable schedules anytime by editing the job properties.

